# Route names are a cross-repo contract

- Route records live in `src/router/routes/*.ts` (core domains) or `src/features/{name}/routes/*.ts` (one product feature), one module per domain; `src/router/index.ts` assembles core modules and spreads `featureRoutes()` from `src/features/registry.ts` (order matters — 404 catch-all last), owns the `beforeEach` guard and `scrollBehavior`.
- **The shell never names a product route module.** `src/features/registry.ts` is the only assembler of feature routes, in registry order; a feature owns its `FeatureModule.routes` and its `boot()` wiring. Core must not import `@/features/{name}/routes/*` (`scripts/check-features.mjs`). A fork drops a feature by deleting its directory, its `src/i18n/features/{name}/` pack and its one line in the registry.
- URL layout: authenticated app under **`/apps/*`**, guest/public at the site root (`/s/*`, payment bounce), auth pages at root.
- **Symbolic route names are consumed by the backend.** Backend menu rows store them and validate against `cored-backend/config/spa-routes.php` (`SpaRouteRegistry`); notification deep links resolve `${route}.view` via `src/utils/notificationTarget.ts`. Renaming or adding a named route = update `config/spa-routes.php` + `MenuSeeder` (when menu-bound) in the same change, plus both integration docs.
- **Guard invariants** (do not regress): one-shot `hydrateShell()` per cold boot with `resetRouterHydration()` on logout, `fetchMe()` re-probe only when the cookie may have arrived from another tab, `guestOnly` → `dashboard.view`, and `revokeCurrentProtectedRoute()` replacing the current protected route with `login.view?redirect=<fullPath>` on logout.
- **Meta flags:** `requiresAuth` (guests → `login.view`), `guestOnly`, `public` (PublicLayout, no auth probe), `breadcrumb`.
- **Breadcrumbs** are declared on route records, not in a central map: `meta.titleKey` (title + default crumb), `meta.breadcrumb.parent` (route name above), `meta.breadcrumb.labelKey` (override). The chain runs self → parent → … → root, capped at 10 hops with a cycle guard; an unresolvable parent ends the chain. A crumb link carries only the params its own path declares.
- **Entity titles:** one `useBreadcrumbTitle()` per detail screen, reading the hydrated record's name (`() => record.value?.name ?? null`), never `route.params.id` and never a translated string. Form-only edit views gate it on `isEdit`. Intentional blanks stay blank (index screens, `activity-log.show`, `error-log.show`, `product-activations.show`).
- Router chunk-load failures are caught by `router.onError` → `chunkLoadFailed` → full-page `ErrorState` with reload.

Details: [docs/routes.md](../../docs/routes.md).
